# apps/admin — platform administration console.
# Copy to .env.local for a host run; the Compose stack supplies these as service environment.
#
# WARNING: Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the shipped bundle at BUILD time. Nothing
# secret may appear here — no session secret, no provider key, no database URL. The bundle is a
# public artefact the moment it is built, regardless of the IP allowlist in front of it.
#
# The consequence of build-time inlining is one artefact per environment: a bundle built against
# staging cannot be promoted to production. Recorded as an open question in architecture.md §18
# — §10.4 implies per-environment builds but no document states it.

# Base URL of the one public API (DR-11, §6.8). Cross-origin by design: admin.<host> calling
# api.<host> is what NFR-65's separate cookie scope requires, and vite.config.ts deliberately
# declines to proxy it away in development.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
